<<<
the agent noun in -er) have v & not f; the statements (or omissions, implying retention of f) cover
===
the agent noun in -er) have *v* & not *f*; the statements (or omissions, implying retention of *f*) cover
>>>

<<<
Where no v form is given, the change to v does not take place, but forms in f are not mentioned except in the (d) or miscellaneous place, unless there is an alternative forminv.
===
Where no *v* form is given, the change to *v* does not take place, but forms in *f* are not mentioned except in the (d) or miscellaneous place, unless there is an alternative form in *v*.
>>>

<<<
When alternatives are given, the first, if either, is better. beef. Pl. beeves oxen, beefs kinds of
